ormat causes an explicit re-embed.\\n+- Keep generation off by default. Bulk generation/backfill is explicit and reports model, prompt version, cost, failures, and coverage.\\n+- Compare retrieval lift, regressions, latency, storage, generation cost, and failure rate against the exact same corpus and query set.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- [ ] A pre-declared residual slice improves materially beyond #517 + #197 without regressing asserted exact/cross-language floors.\\n+- [ ] Generated text never enters lexical search, canonical excerpts, citations, or model-visible historical content.\\n+- [ ] Prompt/model/version changes enumerate stale rows and require an explicit regeneration/re-embed.\\n+- [ ] Provider failure leaves the deterministic baseline operational.\\n+- [ ] Operator readouts expose coverage, failures, cost, and the generated context for inspection without exposing secrets.\\n+- [ ] If no meaningful lift survives the comparison, close this issue as rejected rather than shipping permanent complexity.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+No conversation summary for display, no compaction change, no citation/span selector, no query rewriting, reranker, translated index, fact extraction, or graph memory.\\n+\\n+## Dependencies\\n+\\n+Blocked by #197 and the shipped #517 deterministic anchor. #609 guarantees that even a generated-context hit resolves back to canonical evidence.\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-issue-600.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Build a repeatable long-term-memory evaluation after episodic recall (#194) and indexed Knowledge (#39 → #541) ship, answering:\\n+\\n+> Does the assistant invoke the right memory surface, retrieve and cite the right current source, and fail closed across authorization boundaries?\\n+\\n+This is a versioned llame regression harness, not a leaderboard submission.\\n+\\n+## Native blockers\\n+\\n+- #194 — episodic recall\\n+- #39 — runnable personal Knowledge agent\\n+- #541 — indexed Knowledge retrieval\\n+\\n+If a derived factual-memory corpus ships later, it becomes another blocker and adds write-side hallucination, contradiction, supersession, and deletion probes.\\n+\\n+## Three independent evaluation layers\\n+\\n+### 1. Invocation and routing\\n+\\n+Run with memory tools available but not mandated. Measure:\\n+\\n+- invocation precision/recall;\\n+- correct episodic-vs-Knowledge tool choice;\\n+- correct multi-corpus composition;\\n+- refusal/abstention when no authorized source exists.\\n+\\n+External proactive/context-driven memory benchmarks now exist, so the old claim that every public benchmark force-feeds retrieval is obsolete. llame still needs private fixtures because its tool descriptions, compaction, corpus split, and consent settings are product-specific.\\n+\\n+### 2. Retrieval and citation\\n+\\n+Measure:\\n+\\n+- Recall@K, MRR, nDCG, zero-result rate, per-leg contribution, and exact-vs-ANN recall when applicable;\\n+- bidirectional cross-language recall, mixed-language turns, transliteration, temporal/update questions, and old-but-exact decisions;\\n+- exact-source validity, speaker/time attribution, original-vs-generated-translation labeling, quote support, and multi-span support;\\n+- correctness given invocation, separately from invocation rate.\\n+\\n+Every returned quote must be exact current authorized canonical content. Citation exactness is a gate, not a score utility can trade against.\\n+\\n+### 3. Governance and lifecycle\\n+\\n+Adapt GateMem's threat model as fail-closed gates:\\n+\\n+- cross-tenant and empty-identity retrieval;\\n+- delegated/socially engineered recovery attempts;\\n+- stale source after edit/deletion/permission change;\\n+- owner settings disabling search/read after prior use;\\n+- instruction-shaped historical content;\\n+- compaction recovery without bypassing corpus or authority boundaries.\\n+\\n+Any cross-tenant recall is P0 failure, never an averaged metric.\\n+\\n+## Benchmark use\\n+\\n+- **Primary external:** LongMemEval for temporal, multi-session, update, and abstention abilities.\\n+- **Invocation supplement:** context-driven/proactive retrieval benchmark, adapted rather than copied blindly.\\n+- **Governance gate:** GateMem threat model, not its aggregate score.\\n+- **Smoke only:** LoCoMo; an independent audit found material key/judge/category defects.\\n+- **Private llame corpus:** authoritative release signal for corpus routing, cross-language behavior, compaction, consent, citation, and tenant isolation.\\n+\\n+## Reproducibility requirements\\n+\\n+- [ ] Version and pin answerer model, judge model, judge prompt, tool descriptions, dataset, category inclusion, retrieval depth, token budget, and harness revision.\\n+- [ ] Store judge prompts in the repository.\\n+- [ ] Run model-dependent rows multiple times and report variance/confidence intervals.\\n+- [ ] Separate CI-asserted floors from recorded-only weaknesses.\\n+- [ ] A dataset/harness version change invalidates the old record and requires re-baselining.\\n+- [ ] Provider-billing runs stay off by default behind an explicit environment flag.\\n+- [ ] Preserve per-layer/per-category results; no aggregate hides a security, exact-identifier, cross-language, or citation regression.\\n+\\n+## Corpus requirements\\n+\\n+Include exact identifiers, paraphrases, bidirectional language pairs, code, explicit/vague temporal cues, updates/contradictions, multi-chat synthesis, Knowledge-vs-episodic routing, content removed from active context by compaction, stale/deleted sources, malicious historical instructions, and cross-tenant hard negatives.\\n+\\n+Use public benchmarks for comparability and a private versioned fixture corpus for contamination resistance. Optional operator-local evaluation over real chats/Knowledge never exports source data.\\n+\\n+## Non-goals\\n+\\n+- SOTA or cross-vendor leaderboard claims.\\n+- Letting a stronger answerer/judge substitute for a better memory architecture.\\n+- Replacing the lower-level search retrieval baseline.\\n+- Treating LoCoMo or one aggregate score as a release gate.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n",
